This patch is needed because Chromium C++ modules derive a platform label from
current_os, but the Solaris wrapper reuses the Linux sysroot-style module
layout.

What it does:
- maps Solaris to the Linux module platform naming path

Why it is needed:
- without it, the module platform name does not match the sysroot layout used
  by the Solaris wrapper build

--- a/v8-149.2.0/build/config/c++/modules.gni
+++ b/v8-149.2.0/build/config/c++/modules.gni
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 }
 
 module_platform = "${current_os}-${current_cpu}"
-if (is_chromeos) {
+if (is_chromeos || current_os == "solaris") {
   # ChromeOS uses the linux sysroot.
   module_platform = "linux"
 } else if (is_fuchsia || is_mac || is_linux || is_win) {
